{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges","id":1084022,"title":"Colleges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-26T09:52:20-07:00","id":1084022,"title":"Colleges","content":"Derived from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream\">this</a> thread, and linked conceptually to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1061740-justifications-a-more-developed-beast-society-or-my-first-homebrew-fluff\">this</a> thread.<br /> <br /> The idea is for a Beast Z-splat (or actual Y-Splat? A social Splat, regardless) that leverages the whole &quot;teaching culture&quot;. These would be philosophies and social convention based around teaching certain Lessons. Mechanically, member Beast would gain Kinship (and access to Kinship Nightmares) with the concept behind the College itself, in addition to the inherent advantages being part of a club and shared community brings.<br /> <br /> So, thoughts on this topic? Would would be some good Lessons to base Colleges around? How would this influence the social group? What Nightmares would derived from such philosophies? Or any other comments?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:31:29-07:00","id":1084051,"title":"","content":"EDIT: first part ninja'd by Vent0<br /> <br /> Actually about that name. Given the emphasis on family in Beast, what if we call them Clans? I don't think the werewolves used that name yet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-26-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:35:01-07:00","id":1084052,"title":"","content":"I wonder, might it be better to just call them 'schools'? Both for the teaching connotations, but also for the connotations of groups moving together. Besides, the Dark Dream is often likened to an ocean.<br /> <br /> As for an initial list of ideas for lessons:<ul><li>Humility - You cannot do everything or anything. Hubris is a road to ruin.</li> <li>Cost - Everything has a price, and often that price is steep.</li> <li>Community - Humanity's strength is its unity. Alone, you are weak.</li> <li>Caution - The world is dark and full of terrors. You can avoid them if you are careful, though.</li> <li>Will - What is humanity without the will to carry on, to persevere, to become better, to survive? Dead. That's what.</li> </ul>I'll admit that those are based on the ones in the 'lessons' section of the corebook, but hey. I think they're pretty good.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by MA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:49:48-07:00","id":1084057,"title":"","content":"So many ninjas...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084051#post1084051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: first part ninja'd by Vent0<br /> <br /> Actually about that name. Given the emphasis on family in Beast, what if we call them Clans? I don't think the werewolves used that name yet</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan seems like more of an extension of inherent Family grouping, as opposed an explicitly chosen social group. Might make a good Bloodline-like Z-Splat, though<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084052#post1084052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, might it be better to just call them 'schools'? Both for the teaching connotations, but also for the connotations of groups moving together. Besides, the Dark Dream is often likened to an ocean.<br /> <br /> As for an initial list of ideas for lessons:<ul><li>Humility - You cannot do everything or anything. Hubris is a road to ruin.</li> <li>Cost - Everything has a price, and often that price is steep.</li> <li>Community - Humanity's strength is its unity. Alone, you are weak.</li> <li>Caution - The world is dark and full of terrors. You can avoid them if you are careful, though.</li> <li>Will - What is humanity without the will to carry on, to persevere, to become better, to survive? Dead. That's what.</li> </ul><br /> I'll admit that those are based on the ones in the 'lessons' section of the corebook, but hey. I think they're pretty good.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd by MA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Schools are Leviathan's social grouping. I know, terms get reused all over, but distinction helps, when possible, I think.<br /> <br /> I do like the name of College, as it provides an intellectual contrast to the Beast typically more primal names and themes. It also has the more general alternate definition of &quot;an organized group of professional people with particular aims, duties, and privileges&quot;. Philosophies is a bit long, Deceived took Movements.<br /> <br /> As for groupings, those are nice, but what specific Lessons would make up their &quot;curriculum&quot;? Any ideas on social structure resultant from them? Nightmares?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-26-2017, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:50:13-07:00","id":1084060,"title":"","content":"we could also expand it past teaching lessons to various ways of controlling your place in the primordial story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:00:05-07:00","id":1084066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084060#post1084060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we could also expand it past teaching lessons to various ways of controlling your place in the primordial story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like? What would that be called and how would they be conceptually grouped?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:17:16-07:00","id":1084071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084066#post1084066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like? What would that be called and how would they be conceptually grouped?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that was the point of the &quot;Justifications&quot; (we will rename them something less problematic). At least, that's where the thread was heading: roles in the great story of life that aren't &quot;monster to be slain&quot;. Teacher, Dark Angel, Judge, etc. Sure, not all of them are equally good, but I think a lot of them have merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-26-2017, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:29:48-07:00","id":1084079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084066#post1084066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like? What would that be called and how would they be conceptually grouped?</div> </div> </div> </div>It strikes me that these splats would probably push at the boundaries of 'monsterhood'. Kind of like Life. A counterpart to Family-as-Legend. Maybe...<ul><li><b>The Cunning</b> - Riddlers, deceivers and tricksters. Zahhak and the Serpent in Eden. They teach humility through exposing flaws and weaknesses.</li> <li><b>The Wise</b> - Monsters who nevertheless masters in their field. Wayland, the Witch of Endor and Andvari. They teach costs, as all their gifts come at a price.</li> <li><b>The Mighty</b> - Monsters who are masters of combat and martial endeavour. Grendel and Ravana. They teach the importance of will, for to face them without it is to be defeated.</li> <li><b>The Mothers</b> - Monsters who are a reflection of parenthood, birthing and presiding over litters of their own. Tiamat and Echidna. They teach community by holding up a mirror to humanity's and showing them that <i>strength comes from the many</i>.</li> <li><b>The Haunters</b> - Monsters who <i>are</i>, and that is all they need be. Wendigo and possessing spirits. They teach caution, for they can be anywhere and everywhere. Only vigilance can keep them at bay.</li> </ul>It's kind of similar to Hunger, but these are, after all, artificial divisions created by the Beasts themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-26-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T08:23:16-07:00","id":1084493,"title":"","content":"Thought dump, will refine later:<br /> <br /> <u><b>College of the Joker</b></u><br /> [Desc]<br /> <b>Lessons</b><br /> <i>Laughter is life</i> - [Don't take things so seriously, because you might not be around tomorrow to enjoy them.]<br /> <i>Rules hold you back</i> - [Does the world make sense, or obey the rules society has constructed around it? No! &quot;The only sensible way to live in this world is without rules.&quot;]<br /> <i>No one is different</i> - [Despite airs and pretension, we're only separated by our circumstances. All it takes is one bad day to turn a hero into a villain.]<br /> <b>Kinship</b><br /> [text]<br /> Sample Kinship Nightmares:<ul><li><b>They're All Laughing At You</b> - [Target thinks everyone is mocking them. Makes them distrustful or hostile to everyone, or maybe flee in shame? Other Mental Conditions?]</li> <li><b>You're Just Like Me</b> - [Target is convinced they aren't so different from you, reducing animosity. Social perk? End combat? Prevent Willpower spent to hurt you, since their heart isn't in it?]</li> <li><b>You're Holding Back</b> - [Target is convinced rules are preventing them form completing their goals. Act uninhibited by morals, ethics, or personal code?]</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <u><b>College of the Butterfly</b></u><br /> [Desc]<br /> <b>Lessons</b><br /> <i>Small efforts can lead to great change</i> - [The merest wing-flap can lead to a hurricane.]<br /> <i>Repercussions can't always be seen</i> - [If a wing flap can spark a wind storm, what makes you think you an predict the effects of your own actions?]<br /> <i>Change can be transformative</i> - [Like the difference between a caterpillar and a butterfly, who we were doesn't have to dictate who we will be.]<br /> <b>Kinship</b><br /> [text]<br /> Sample Kinship Nightmares:<ul><li><b>Just As I Planned</b> - [Target is convinced that even your minor involvement led to this inevitable outcome. Beaten Down Tilt, since opposition is pointless? Paranoia Condition?]</li> <li><b>Look What You Have Done</b> - [Target is overwhelmed at the unintended consequences of their actions. May cause choice paralysis? Force them into odd behavior in the belief it will get what they want?]</li> <li><b>This Isn't Even My Final Form</b> - [Target is convinced that what they see is not the end of things. May confuse another target with you?]</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-27-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:35:47-07:00","id":1084527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084071#post1084071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that was the point of the &quot;Justifications&quot; (we will rename them something less problematic). At least, that's where the thread was heading: roles in the great story of life that aren't &quot;monster to be slain&quot;. Teacher, Dark Angel, Judge, etc. Sure, not all of them are equally good, but I think a lot of them have merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow that is a lot better then my original idea.<br /> <br /> Also, another way of grouping colleges could be how they teach- teaching the masses/the individuals, teaching in the waking world/the dream,teaching blatently/subtly, etc? or something like that? It could fit in with 2nd editions more &quot;make your own&quot; approach to y-splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:49:10-07:00","id":1084531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084527#post1084527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow that is a lot better then my original idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>you don't give yourself enough credit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T14:20:25-07:00","id":1084696,"title":"","content":"<u><b>College of the Throne</b></u><br /> [Desc]<br /> <b>Lessons</b><br /> <i>Strength leads the weak</i> - [The best at their job are in charge of directing those inferior - anything else is foolish.]<br /> <i>Power unused is power wasted</i> - [If you can act, but choose not to, it is any different that lacking the ability to act in the first place?]<br /> <i>Know your own strength</i> - [You'll never know what you can accomplish unless you push yourself. At the same time, reaching beyond your grasp brings ruin to all around you.]<br /> <b>Kinship</b><br /> [text]<br /> Sample Kinship Nightmares:<ul><li><b>Kneel Before <s>Zod</s> Me!</b> - [Target submits to your authority and superiority. Cover any gaps left by You Must Obey?]</li> <li><b>Give Me Your All</b> - [Target becomes terrified of failure, exerting themselves beyond normal limits. Increase willpower effect? Inflict harm from over-strain in addition to other effects?]</li> <li><b>Know Your Place</b> - [Target understands where they sit in the current social and power dynamic. Beaten Down vs &quot;superiors&quot;? Bonus vs &quot;inferiors&quot;?]</li> </ul><br /> <hr /><br /> Any feedback and what I have so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:27:16-07:00","id":1084730,"title":"","content":"I like them! Although on a very minor point &quot;You're just like me&quot; doesn't seem very nightmarish as is- &quot;Only I like you&quot; or something like that, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:36:21-07:00","id":1084734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084730#post1084730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like them! Although on a very minor point &amp;quot;You're just like me&amp;quot; doesn't seem very nightmarish as is- &amp;quot;Only I like you&amp;quot; or something like that, maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can see what inspired that College, right? Just imagine a Beast saying that to a Hunter (or Joker saying it to Batman). The idea that you are every bit as much of a monster as what stands before you. Or, for those already monsters, that you aren't any better than what you are fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:53:07-07:00","id":1084738,"title":"","content":"Ah, I missed that inspiration. Still, it seems a bit odd for &quot;you're a horrifying monster&quot; to lead to social bonuses? It's rarely something that ends with friendship, or even alliance, in the inspirations. Something that prevents the person working against the beast, maybe?<br /> <br /> I like what you have so far, to avoid derailing this into a conversation about one potential nightmare. Any idea on how you would join a college? It seems a bit unthematic for it to be an organisation in the conventional sense, at least to me. Maybe there are &quot;super-lairs&quot; of the colleges/concepts behind them and linking your lair to them is how it works. It would also help make the primordial dream a little less empty- it is possible to meet people in a neutral dreamscape outside of one of your lairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T16:07:09-07:00","id":1084744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1084022-colleges?p=1084738#post1084738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I missed that inspiration. Still, it seems a bit odd for &quot;you're a horrifying monster&quot; to lead to social bonuses? It's rarely something that ends with friendship, or even alliance, in the inspirations. Something that prevents the person working against the beast, maybe?<br /> <br /> I like what you have so far, to avoid derailing this into a conversation about one potential nightmare. Any idea on how you would join a college? It seems a bit unthematic for it to be an organisation in the conventional sense, at least to me. Maybe there are &quot;super-lairs&quot; of the colleges/concepts behind them and linking your lair to them is how it works. It would also help make the primordial dream a little less empty- it is possible to meet people in a neutral dreamscape outside of one of your lairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I had the general idea of the fear and the Quote/name - mechanics will come later.<br /> <br /> For joining a College, it is pretty much encounter it as a philosophy (independently, or by meeting another member) and committing to teaching those Lessons - that those things have Meaning, and define Who You Are.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, it might be represented by &quot;paying&quot; (dedicating) one of your Chambers as Tuition/Entry Fee, where upon it joins the Campus - an extended meta-Lair/Hive accessible by all Members. This would also, mechanically restrict it to Beasts Lair 2 and up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/